.TH CHANGELOG-LOG 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog log \- display changelog fragments in git-log style format with pagination
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog log
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBlog\fR command displays fragment files in a structured, git-log-style format suitable for reviewing accumulated changes. It provides interactive pagination support and configurable page sizes for navigating large numbers of fragments.

This is useful for previewing what will appear in release notes before generating them, reviewing recent changes, or auditing fragment content across multiple directories.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Fragment directory to display. Defaults to "changelogs/fragments" in the current project root.
.PP
Can specify multiple directories using separate -d flags or comma-separated paths.

.TP
\fB\-\-page\-size\fR=\fIN\fR
Number of entries per page when displaying output. Defaults to 10 if not specified. Set to -1 for unlimited (no pagination).

.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Enable interactive pagination mode with keypress navigation:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSpace\fR or \fBf\fR \- Next page
.IP \(bu 2
\bBb\fR or \fBSpace\fR \- Previous page
.IP \(bu 2
\fBq\fR or \fBCtrl+C\fR \- Quit
.IP \(bu 2
\fB<\fR or \fBH\fR \- First page
.IP \(bu 2
\fB>\fR or \fBL\fR \- Last page
.RE

.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-notes-dir\fR=\fIDIR\fR
Additional fragment directories to merge into the display. Can be specified multiple times for multiple notes directories. Useful for viewing fragments organized by subsystem or team.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.PP
The log command displays fragments in a structured format showing:

.TP
.B Fragment Header:
.nf
    --- [Issue ID] Category (YYYY-MM-DD) ---
.fi

.TP
.B Fragment Content:
.nf
    Title: Human-readable title for the fragment

    Body:
    Fragment body text content here...

    Metadata:
      author: developer@example.com  (if present)
      issue_type: bugfix              (if categorized)
.fi

.TP
.B Pagination Indicator:
.nf
    Page X of Y (Press space for next, q to quit)
.fi
.SH FRAGMENT SORTING
.PP
Fragments are displayed in chronological order (newest first), matching the order they would appear in release notes. Within each day, fragments are sorted by category priority:

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
1. Breaking Changes / Porting Guide
.IP \(bu 2
2. Major Changes
.IP \(bu 2
3. Deprecated Features
.IP \(bu 2
4. Removed Features
.IP \(bu 2
5. Bugfixes
.IP \(bu 2
6. Security Fixes
.IP \(bu 2
7. Minor Changes
.IP \(bu 2
8. Known Issues
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Display fragments with default pagination:
.nf
    changelog log
.fi

.TP
View all fragments without pagination (useful for piping):
.nf
    changelog log --page-size -1 | less
.fi

.TP
Interactive browsing with custom page size:
.nf
    changelog log --interactive --page-size 20
.fi

.TP
Display fragments from multiple directories:
.nf
    changelog log \\
        -d changelogs/fragments/core \\
        -d changelogs/notes/community \\
        --interactive
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate release notes from fragments (uses same sorting)
.TP
\fBchangelog-add(8)\fR \- Create new fragment files
.TP
\fBgit-log(1)\fR \- Similar git log command with comparable pagination features
